<title>USA: US Defense Stockpile sells germanium in tender.</title>
<headline>US Defense Stockpile sells germanium in tender.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Defense National Stockpile Center said it sold 359 kilograms of germanium worth $503,535 by tender Thursday.</p>
<p>The largest award under the tender went to Tennelec/Nucleus Inc, of Oak Ridge, Tennessee which took 275 kilgrams at a unit price of $1,401 a kilogram.</p>
<p>The next tender will be held on May 27.</p>
<p>((--New York Commodities Desk, 212-859-1640))</p>
</text>
